<h2
id="computer-based-testing-facility-cbtf"><a name="syllabus"></a>Computer-Based
Testing Facility (CBTF)</h2>
<p>Designated exams for this course will be administered through the
Computer-Based Testing Facility (CBTF) in Gilmer Hall 490A. The CBTF
provides a secure, professionally proctored testing environment and
allows students the flexibility to schedule exams within an
instructor-defined testing window. Students are responsible for
reserving an exam appointment and following CBTF testing policies and
procedures. Additional instructions will be provided before each
exam.</p>
<h2
id="accounts-prairietest-and-prairielearn"><a name="lectures"></a>Accounts
(PrairieTest and PrairieLearn)</h2>
<p>Within the first week of class, <strong>every student needs to create
an account</strong> on two related systems:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://us.prairietest.com">Priarie Test</a>: Prairie Test
is used to make exam reservations before an exam and to actually take
your exam once you arrive at the CBTF.</li>
<li><a href="https://us.prairielearn.com">Prairie Learn</a>: Prairie
Learn is used to as a portal mostly for viewing your grades AFTER an
exam has occurred.</li>
</ul>
<p>The <strong>instructor will upload a course roster within one week of
class starting and add you to our course instance</strong> so that these
systems will work correctly. However, each student still needs to create
their own account themselves.</p>
<h2 id="practice-exam"><a name="textbook"></a>Practice Exam</h2>
<p>Early in the semester (around week 3), there will be a low-stakes
practice exam designed to ease everybody into the procedure of using the
CBTF. Please review the document below for information regarding this
practice exam.</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="./CBTFSimulationExamInformation.pdf">CBTF Practice Exam
Information</a></li>
</ul>
